1. Scope and preserved permissions

“Legacy Baseline” means commit 262e60ec8e9814ddaca1b9e81c9f63bb90b858e0
of https://github.com/hendrillara/akoma. Its code remains available under
licenses/MIT-legacy.txt. Previously published CC0 material remains available
under its original dedication. Those permissions are not revoked or restricted
by this licence, including for future recipients of that material.

“Covered Material” means new, copyright-protected original code, documentation
and other contributions owned by the Licensor, first published in this
repository after the Legacy Baseline under this licence. In a modified legacy
file, only new protectable contributions are Covered Material; the unchanged
legacy material retains its earlier terms. A new commit, release number,
repository name, format conversion or regeneration does not by itself make
legacy or public-domain material Covered Material.

Excluded from Covered Material are statutory and other public-domain texts,
previously CC0-dedicated material, third-party dependencies, third-party source
