Subject to sections 3 and 4, the Licensor grants a worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free permission to use, reproduce, study, modify and distribute Covered
Material solely for personal use, education or research without a commercial
purpose. This includes noncommercial publications and noncommercial research
demonstrations. Rights not expressly granted are reserved.

“Commercial Use” includes use in a paid or revenue-generating product or service;
client work or consulting; business operations or internal professional use;
and use to develop, operate or improve a commercial offering, including a free,
advertising-supported or indirectly monetised offering. Organisational or
nonprofit status alone does not determine whether a use is noncommercial.
Research principally intended to benefit a commercial offering is Commercial
Use. Request a written clarification from the Licensor if the purpose is unclear.

3. Attribution and redistribution

When distributing Covered Material or making a product, service, research
publication or integration using it available to others, retain this licence,
applicable copyright notices and third-party notices, identify your changes,
and include either of these credits with a clickable link where supported:

“Uses Akoma by Hendril Lara — https://github.com/hendrillara/akoma”
“Utiliza Akoma, de Hendril Lara — https://github.com/hendrillara/akoma”

The credit must be reasonably discoverable in the product's credits/about page
or integration documentation. For a backend-only service, include it in the
API/integration documentation supplied to its consumers. For an internal tool,
include it in the documentation available to its users. For a publication,
include it in acknowledgments or references. Private personal use requires
retaining the notices in the copy, not publishing a public announcement.

Do not imply endorsement by the Licensor. You may not remove notices or offer
recipients broader rights to Covered Material than this licence grants.
Redistributed Covered Material remains subject to these terms; this does not
require unrelated software to adopt this licence. Distribution under this
section must itself be noncommercial unless authorised under section 4.

4. Commercial permission and royalties

Commercial Use of Covered Material is not licensed by the noncommercial grant.
Before starting Commercial Use, obtain a separate written commercial agreement
signed by the Licensor and the customer. That agreement must identify the
licensed material and use, term, royalty rate or royalty amounts, calculation
base, reporting and payment schedule, and the attribution placement.

Royalties are negotiated per customer; this document sets no public rate or
automatic invoice. Paying a donation, buying integration/support services, or
sending an inquiry does not grant commercial rights unless a signed agreement
expressly does so. Permission under that agreement is conditional on compliance
with its royalty payment terms and the attribution requirement in section 3.
Attribution remains required for commercial use. Any exception requires a
separate express written amendment signed by the Licensor.

Commercial enquiries: https://github.com/hendrillara/akoma/issues/new
See COMMERCIAL.md for the process. Do not submit confidential terms or client
data in a public issue; arrange a private channel before negotiating them.

5. Termination and reinstatement

The noncommercial permission terminates automatically if its conditions are
violated. For a first noncommercial breach, it is reinstated when the breach
is fully cured within 30 days of discovery. A Commercial Use without a signed
commercial agreement is not authorised by this cure provision. Commercial
agreement remedies and termination are governed by that agreement. Termination
does not affect independent legacy MIT, CC0, public-domain or third-party rights.

